{"id": "EUVD-2026-103565", "enisaUuid": "591ad289-5c49-3040-82f4-47489bdd44fa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: Properly handle NULL pointer in dat_cond_set_storage_key()\n\nSome callers pass NULL as oldkey. Calling page_cond_set_storage_key()\nwill cause that NULL pointer to get dereferenced.\n\nFix by checking for NULL and assigning the pointer to a dummy local\nvariable to avoid crashes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:22", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/75867536746ab2d034488a6a93ee6cde83553342", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/88e22ffd1e46b95e40a6afabe486deb1d31a3ae1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7vxp-j7m5-7gf4", "CVE-2026-98651"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "49962d9f-5dd0-39bf-8b7e-b96db7db13be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "60dd8230-ed9a-3ac6-96a7-8faaedbcccbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8e03e8316eb242af307d1c789d09f1a1457cf9a3 <75867536746ab2d034488a6a93ee6cde83553342"}, {"id": "c7f80fe0-9b93-394b-83b4-8d113e16db4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "cd258ace-3953-32aa-9cdf-05beff317769", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "d344dd4c-f5aa-3a55-a0b1-75f61cb4456a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8e03e8316eb242af307d1c789d09f1a1457cf9a3 <88e22ffd1e46b95e40a6afabe486deb1d31a3ae1"}, {"id": "ff715d1a-a0f9-3ee8-88b7-49ba9f812a59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "498985fb-26e9-38bb-b092-05a022786d32", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}